Z||000007||Alex4mula||12-19-2001||01:20 PM||||Beautiful setup ;-) No, it won't work in Florida  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>Would love to see something like what they offer for the Hondas with a shaft driving the blower in the other side of the engine. Only if they had sold 1-2M instead of 300K+ Fieros...<P>------------------<BR>    Alex4mula<BR>:) Red-Original Owner & White-1/94 with PM (:||||reg||1
Z||000008||lou||12-19-2001||02:33 PM||||I suggest you place a second tensioner between the alternator and water pump as there is not enough belt surface on the waterpump pulley, and you will overheat. if you have a problem finding a 5 groove belt that is long enough  you can always cut a six grove down to five.<p>[This message has been edited by lou (edited 12-19-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||88VortechGT||12-19-2001||03:25 PM||||Thanks for the input but this system has already been installed in another car in Canada and they had no over heating problems.||||reg||1
Z||000010||lou||12-19-2001||03:31 PM||||Just speaking from personal experience, it is a LOT easier to do it while the engine is out of the car. <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.4u2buy.com/cars/BELT.jpg"> ||||reg||1
